  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1238 AM CDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nA strong high pressure ridge currently sitting across the \nsoutheastern U.S. will shift to the west. This will leave our area \ncloser to the center of the high pressure. As a result, hot and dry \nconditions will continue through the end of the work week. By Sunday \nand Monday, a couple of embedded disturbances aloft will cruise \nthrough the region. This will act to weaken the ridge and allow for \na medium chance (30-50%) for rain. A weak cold frontal boundary may \nbe just strong enough to drop temperatures a few degrees early next \nweeks. Highs appear to be in the lower 90s during this timeframe.",
